{"causes": ["His noble birth into the ancient and distinguished House of Lévis provided him with immediate access to military and courtly careers in 18th-century France.", "The ongoing European power struggles, including the War of the Austrian Succession, created demand for experienced military commanders and astute diplomats.", "King Louis XV's need for loyal and capable servants to navigate complex international relations propelled figures like Mirepoix into positions of influence."], "effects": ["His diplomatic service as ambassador to Vienna and London contributed to France's foreign policy objectives in the mid-18th century.", "His military commands during various European wars helped to shape French strategic deployments and tactical decisions on critical fronts.", "His elevation to Marshal of France in 1757 solidified his family's prestige and confirmed his personal legacy as a leading military figure of his generation."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "louis-xv", "sourceName": "Louis XV", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "gaston-pierre-de-lvis", "targetName": "Gaston Pierre de Lévis", "context": "Louis XV appointed Gaston Pierre de Lévis as his ambassador to Vienna and London, and later elevated him to Marshal of France, critically shaping his career."}, {"sourceSlug": "gaston-pierre-de-lvis", "sourceName": "Gaston Pierre de Lévis", "verb": "PARTICIPATES_IN", "targetSlug": "war-of-the-austrian-succession", "targetName": "War of the Austrian Succession", "context": "Gaston Pierre de Lévis distinguished himself as a lieutenant-general in the French army during the War of the Austrian Succession (1740-1748)."}, {"sourceSlug": "gaston-pierre-de-lvis", "sourceName": "Gaston Pierre de Lévis", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "paris-france", "targetName": "Paris, France", "context": "Gaston Pierre de Lévis's significant diplomatic appointments and courtly life largely transpired in Paris, the center of French power."}, {"sourceSlug": "gaston-pierre-de-lvis